law.text:
		A certificate of membership shall be invalid if:

The certificate holder was ill at the time the certificate was procured;


Any person concerned in the procurement of the certificate had reason to believe that the illness existed at that time;


The illness continued to the death of the certificate holder and was a contributing cause of death;


Health questions were not asked on the application for coverage; and


The certificate holder died within sixty days from the date the certificate was issued.
